~ start
The room is small, barely furnished, with a few boxes stacked against the wall. You drop your bag on the bed and glance around. This is home now. The city outside feels distant, muffled by the quiet hum of restrictions. No welcoming parties, no campus tours—just you, a laptop, and the uncertainty of starting fresh in the middle of a pandemic.

Your new apartment is small but enough. Boxes are scattered across the floor, waiting to be unpacked, but your mind is elsewhere. Tomorrow, classes start—online, of course. Meeting people, making friends, and navigating student life in a pandemic… it's going to be an experience unlike any other.

For now, you take a deep breath and look out the window. This is your new life.
